.TH "ATOMDNS" 1 "September 2025" "atomdns" "atomdns authors"

.SH "ATOMDNS"
.PP
\fIatomdns\fP \- DNS nameserver that runs handlers

.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
\fIatomdns\fP \fB[\-c FILE]\fP \fB[\-p PORT]\fP \fB[OPTION]\fP...

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
atomdns is a DNS server that chains handlers. Each handler handles a DNS feature, like serve zone files,
transfering those to secondaries or just exporting metrics. There are many handlers, each described in their
respective manual pages.

.PP
Available options:

.TP
\fB\-c\fP, \fB\-conf\fP \fBFILE\fP
specify Corefile to load, if not given atomdns will look for a \fB\fCConffile\fR in the current
directory.
.TP
\fB\-p\fP, \fB\-\-port\fP \fBPORT\fP
override default port (53) to listen on.
.TP
\fB\-handlers\fP
list all handlers and quit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fP, \fB\-version\fP
show version and quit.
.TP
\fB\-cpuprofile\fP
write a cpu profile to "cpu.out".


